title an escape above 377 names no byte

# NOT in the cross-parser diff yet, because the two parsers disagree
# about it and the C side is the one that is right.
#
# Three octal digits reach 511; a byte does not. The C parser rejects
# \400 and up. The reference parser currently accepts it and produces
# a character with code 256 -- not a byte at all -- which re-encodes
# to "\400" in the dump and so looks entirely fine while being
# nothing a file name could hold. The same escape in C would truncate
# to NUL, which is worse than wrong: it would smuggle in the one byte
# the NUL check exists to reject.
#
# Proposed message, matching the shape of the other two:
#
#   leaf 'over\400flow' has an escape above \377, which names no byte
#
# Move this into devcheck/treecases/ the moment the reference rejects
# it, and delete devcheck/pending/ once it is empty. treecheck.sh
# prints what is waiting here on every run, so it cannot be forgotten
# quietly.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: over\400flow
